(170769, 8275, 4628, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gracechild7:</b></div><hr/><i>I like the photo, but I am confused about the title...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The title has a personal meaning to me. I wouldnt expect it to mean anything to any one else, though.</td>', 'Originally posted by Gracechild7:I like the photo, but I am confused about the title...  The title has a personal meaning to me. I wouldnt expect it to mean anything to any one else, though.', '2002-12-12 04:01:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(172564, 8211, 245, '<td valign="top">I realy like this photo, the only nit I can pick is the slight purple fringey effect on the upper left edges of the petals, you may have done it intentionally, but it reminds me of chromatic aberrarion. I would have tried pushing it all into reds/oranges. Right now it looks kinda low tech, and purer reds might help legitamize the deliberate blow-out and softness... I am always surprised when people can''t just let vagueness and softness please the eye as it is.</td>', 'I realy like this photo, the only nit I can pick is the slight purple fringey effect on the upper left edges of the petals, you may have done it intentionally, but it reminds me of chromatic aberrarion. I would have tried pushing it all into reds/oranges. Right now it looks kinda low tech, and purer reds might help legitamize the deliberate blow-out and softness... I am always surprised when people can''t just let vagueness and softness please the eye as it is.', '2002-12-15 16:49:46.000000', NULL, 0);
<br/> <br/>BTW, having the same camera as yours, I''m suprised at the level of focus you got from this macro shot. Nice!<br/> <br/>Shadow</td>', 'the picture speaks for itself and gets the message across pretty well. I guess saturating or adjusting the hue for RED may help improve this one further from a 5 to 6. Just my opinion.  BTW, having the same camera as yours, I''m suprised at the level of focus you got from this macro shot. Nice! Shadow', '2003-05-04 03:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
