(152957, 7993, 4625, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who left comments, With comments like these my score doesn''t dissapoint me so much :-P I took a risk doing something "Artistic" in a challenge like macro... I knew I did too... I had some other macro shots that were of the same image, but closer up of the water drop. If you want to see my outtakes you can find them here //gaze.myparadise.org/pin.htm <br/><br/>I chose my favorite photo, I guess I should have picked a more technical shot, but I really liked this one for it''s artistic value... I''m just glad a few of you enjoyed my shot :) thanks again fro the comments.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who left comments, With comments like these my score doesn''t dissapoint me so much :-P I took a risk doing something "Artistic" in a challenge like macro... I knew I did too... I had some other macro shots that were of the same image, but closer up of the water drop. If you want to see my outtakes you can find them here //gaze.myparadise.org/pin.htm I chose my favorite photo, I guess I should have picked a more technical shot, but I really liked this one for it''s artistic value... I''m just glad a few of you enjoyed my shot :) thanks again fro the comments.', '2002-11-18 01:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(152958, 7994, 3080, '<td valign="top">Well isn''t he creepy!  Is he one of those pill bugs?  Your focus is very nice.  The detail you show us here is just great.  I love the little shell like plating around the edge.  Thanks for doing this shot from his underside, I don''t think the other side would be this interesting.  The lighting is nice.  I wasn''t for sure about the colored tint, but as I think about it, black and white wouldn''t look as nice, neither would sepia.  I think being a bug, the greenish tint works nicely.  Great shot. Good luck in the challenge. ~Hbunch7187~</td>', 'Well isn''t he creepy!  Is he one of those pill bugs?  Your focus is very nice.  The detail you show us here is just great.  I love the little shell like plating around the edge.  Thanks for doing this shot from his underside, I don''t think the other side would be this interesting.  The lighting is nice.  I wasn''t for sure about the colored tint, but as I think about it, black and white wouldn''t look as nice, neither would sepia.  I think being a bug, the greenish tint works nicely.  Great shot. Good luck in the challenge. ~Hbunch7187~', '2002-11-11 02:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
