(156204, 8299, 1143, '<td valign="top">Man. I wish I were at the beach  *sigh*  Beautiful sky and water back there! It''s an interesting shot. I think it''d be cool if you had done a portrait type shot with part of the shell in the lower left and the sky and water behind it. The repetition created by the shells is cool.  I do like the shot as is (tho the focus seems a bit soft even in the foreground) but for a macro challenge I think it would be best to focus on just one shell.  ~indigo997</td>', 'Man. I wish I were at the beach  *sigh*  Beautiful sky and water back there! It''s an interesting shot. I think it''d be cool if you had done a portrait type shot with part of the shell in the lower left and the sky and water behind it. The repetition created by the shells is cool.  I do like the shot as is (tho the focus seems a bit soft even in the foreground) but for a macro challenge I think it would be best to focus on just one shell.  ~indigo997', '2002-11-12 01:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(156205, 8299, 806, '<td valign="top">interesting idea.... i''d like my eye to be led in the opposite diagonal, i.e to the right. love the contrasts and set up. brings me to a paradise.</td>', 'interesting idea.... i''d like my eye to be led in the opposite diagonal, i.e to the right. love the contrasts and set up. brings me to a paradise.', '2002-11-12 16:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
